    [31m**Follows**: the early notice **B-1** in `valuejs-outbound-2026-07-28-o18-watercolor-toggle-loupe.md`[39m
    [31m§B — *\"If the wave mechanism lands as a variant of your aurora/gradient primitives rather than[39m
    [31mdemo-side, a follow-up ask will carry the exact shape.\"* This is that follow-up.[39m
    [31m**Authority for the branch**: `W6.md` X.W6.e — *\"If the wave mechanism proves to belong inside the[39m
    [31mglass gradient/aurora primitive, it leaves as a marked BJ ask (same two-way falsifier as d2).\"*[39m
    [31m**Machine oracle**: `npx playwright test e2e/smoke/views/gradient.spec.ts -g \"gradient selector aurora\"`.[39m
    [31mIt re-runs the census in §2 on every run and **reds the day a fitting primitive ships** — so this letter[39m
    [31mcannot outlive the fact that justifies it — and it reds equally if the wave animates the ramp locally.·[39m
    [31m---·[39m
    [31m## 1. The mandate, verbatim·[39m
    [31mOwner, 2026-07-28 (MT-F041): *\"let's plan to add a bit of dyannism to the gradient selector--it should[39m
    [31mbecome a SUBTLE aurora insofar as the gradient waves a bit.\"* Standing constraints (`W6.md` X.W6.e):[39m
    [31mconsume the shared field/motion law from `@mkbabb/glass-ui/aurora`; **no new animation species**; **no[39m
    [31mprivate rAF loop**; PRM honoured **structurally** (declared inside[39m
    [31m`@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`), never by leaning on the global reduce guard.·[39m
    [31m## 2. The census — why no published primitive fits (re-run by the gate)·[39m
    [31m`@mkbabb/glass-ui` **7.0.0**, 74 published subpaths. `./aurora` (`dist/components/aurora/index.d.ts`,[39m
    [31msha256 `6c9b1bce53361513260ccea723826dd724604d6cc220a58383856f0c1694466d`) publishes:·[39m
    [31m| export | what it is | fits a strip wave? |[39m
    [31m|---|---|---|[39m
    [31m| `Aurora` (component) | the full-field painterly background: one WebGL2 canvas sized to its container | **no** — see (a), (b) |[39m
    [31m| `useAurora`, `createAurora`, `useCursorInteraction` | the WebGL runtime and its pointer bridge | **no** — the same substrate |[39m
    [31m| `resolveRenderMode`, `isSoftwareWebGLRenderer` | the substrate selector (`\"webgl\" \\| \"css\" \\| \"auto\"`) | — (a guard, not a surface) |[39m
    [31m| `deriveAurora`, `paletteToCssGradient`, `cssToOklch`, `flattenPalette`, … | colour helpers: palette derivation and a **static** CSS gradient string | **no** — no motion |[39m
    [31m| `auroraFallbackGround`, `sampleAuroraField`, `nucleiFieldStatic` | the **static** first-frame ground | **no** — no motion |[39m
    [31m| `DEFAULT_AURORA_CONFIG`, atoms, presets | configuration | — |·[39m
    [31mAnd the stylesheet: `grep -rhoE '@keyframes [a-z-]*aurora[a-z-]*' dist` → **0**. The aurora motion[39m
    [31mvocabulary exists **only** inside the WebGL runtime.·[39m
    [31mThree measured facts close the local routes:·[39m
    [31m- **(a) The CSS substrate is still.** `renderMode.d.ts`: a software rasteriser takes the `\"css\"`[39m
    [31m  substrate — *\"the static gradient placeholder\"* — by the producer's own safe default, and the named[39m
    [31m  escape `forceWebGLUnderSoftwareRaster` exists *\"for a deterministic test that ACCEPTS the[39m
    [31m  per-composite raster cost\"*, not for a product surface. A strip that waves only on a GPU is a strip[39m
    [31m  that never waves on the smoke cell and on every GPU-blocklisted device (value.js's own[39m
    [31m  `o26-aurora-perceptibility` records the same: the atmosphere is a still under headless GL).[39m
    [31m- **(b) A second full-field WebGL canvas per gradient pane** is a second GPU context on the route that[39m
    [31m  already hosts the atmosphere's — for a ~40 px strip.[39m
    [31m- **(c) The rail's one-axis law forbids moving the ramp.** The gradient rail paints each colour at the[39m
    [31m  ordinal its handle sits on (X.W6.a a3/a4; X.W6.c c2: the ghost, the caret and the rail agree to the[39m
    [31m  sample). A wave that displaces colour along the axis would put a colour under a handle that does not[39m
    [31m  own it. The motion therefore has to live on an axis the ordinal does not — a veil, a luminance drift,[39m
    [31m  a silhouette — which is a new primitive, not a configuration of `Aurora`.·[39m
    [31mA consumer-side cure would therefore mint either a new `@keyframes` species (banned) or a private rAF[39m
    [31mloop (banned). **The mechanism belongs to the producer.**·[39m
    [31m## 3. The ask·[39m
    [31mA **strip-scale aurora motion primitive** in `./aurora` (or a sibling subpath), one of:·[39m
    [31m1. **`<AuroraStrip>`** — wraps a caller-supplied background (a CSS gradient string, or `OklchStop[]`)[39m
    [31m   and overlays the aurora field's drift as a **veil** that never displaces the caller's colours along[39m
    [31m   the strip's long axis (luminance / chroma breathing, or a gently waving silhouette); or[39m
    [31m2. **a utility + keyframes pair** (e.g. `glass-aurora-drift`) applicable to any element as an extra[39m
    [31m   background layer, with the drift's tempo and amplitude from the motion tokens (`--motion-tempo`,[39m
    [31m   the aurora breath).·[39m
    [31mEither way, the contract we need:·[39m
    [31m- a **CSS substrate that moves** (no WebGL context per strip), so the wave exists on every renderer;[39m
    [31m- motion declared **inside `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`** in the producer's own stylesheet[39m
    [31m  (still, not merely slowed, under reduce);[39m
    [31m- subtle by default (the owner's word), with one documented amplitude knob;[39m
    [31m- no colour displacement along the long axis (the one-axis law above).·[39m
    [31m**Consumer commitment**: value.js composes it on the gradient rail (`GradientStopEditor.vue`'s[39m
    [31m`.gradient-rail`) and nowhere else in this wave; the e1 oracle then flips to the composing branch and[39m
    [31mmeasures the motion as a settled-frame delta at a fixed colour.·[39m
    [31m*Sent by the value.js X-W6 wave (Repair 1), 2026-09-22. Reply folds per E13.*·[39m
